            </div>
            
          </div>
          <p class="mb-0 mt-1 search-abstract">Partial fraction decomposition is a fundamental technique in mathematics where products of rational functions can be expressed as sums of fractions. While rational functions have been used in various cryptographic constructions, their rich algebraic structure has not been systematically explored as a direct foundation for building cryptographic primitives. In this work, we describe and exploit two key properties of partial fraction decomposition:  
(1) the decomposition property itself,...</p>
        </div>

