          <p class="mb-0 mt-1 search-abstract">Update: We retract the claim that main construction in the paper is cryptographically secure. In particular, the trapdoor functions generated in Algorithm 1 from three dimensional tensors are efficiently distinguishable from random tensors, since their two dimensional slices (in the longest dimension) are rank deficient. We leave the article as a record, in hopes that some of the techniques are useful in other contexts.

Weyman and Zelevinsky generalised Vandermonde matrices to higher...</p>
