          <small class="ms-auto">Last updated: 2023-07-18</small>
        </div>
        <div class="ms-md-4">
          <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-md-row justify-content-between">
            <div>
              <strong>Handling Adaptive Compromise for Practical Encryption Schemes</strong>
              <div class="mt-1"><span class="fst-italic">Joseph Jaeger, Nirvan Tyagi</span></div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="float-end mt-1 ms-md-3">
              <small class="badge category category-SECRETKEY">Secret-key cryptography</small>
            </div>
            
          </div>
          <p class="mb-0 mt-1 search-abstract">We provide a new definitional framework capturing the multi-user security of encryption schemes and pseudorandom functions in the face of adversaries that can adaptively compromise users&#39; keys. We provide a sequence of results establishing the security of practical symmetric encryption schemes under adaptive compromise in the random oracle or ideal cipher model. The bulk of analysis complexity for adaptive compromise security is relegated to the analysis of lower-level primitives such as...</p>
        </div>

