              <strong>Broadcast Secret-Sharing, Bounds and Applications</strong>
              <div class="mt-1"><span class="fst-italic">Ivan Damgård, Kasper Green Larsen, Sophia Yakoubov</span></div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="float-end mt-1 ms-md-3">
              <small class="badge category category-FOUNDATIONS">Foundations</small>
            </div>
            
          </div>
          <p class="mb-0 mt-1 search-abstract">Consider a sender S and a group and of n recipients. S holds a secret message m of length l bits and the goal is to allow S to create a secret sharing of m with privacy threshold t among the recipients, by broadcasting a single message c to the recipients. Our goal is to do this with information theoretic security in a model with a simple form of correlated randomness. Namely, for each subset A of recipients of size q, S may share a secret random bit string with all recipients in A. We call...</p>
        </div>

