              <div class="mt-1"><span class="fst-italic">Daniel Jost, Ueli Maurer, Marta Mularczyk</span></div>
            </div>
            
          </div>
          <p class="mb-0 mt-1 search-abstract">In the era of mass surveillance and information breaches, privacy of Internet communication, and messaging in particular, is a growing concern. As secure messaging protocols are executed on the not-so-secure end-user devices, and because their sessions are long-lived, they aim to guarantee strong security even if secret states and local randomness can be exposed.

The most basic security properties, including forward secrecy, can be achieved using standard techniques such as authenticated...</p>
