            <div>
              <strong>Cryptographic Constructions Supporting Implicit Data Integrity</strong>
              <div class="mt-1"><span class="fst-italic">Michael Kounavis, David Durham, Sergej Deutsch</span></div>
            </div>
            
          </div>
          <p class="mb-0 mt-1 search-abstract">We study a methodology for supporting data integrity called \lq implicit integrity\rq $\&gt;$ and present cryptographic constructions supporting it.  Implicit integrity allows for corruption detection without producing, storing or verifying mathematical summaries of the content such as MACs and ICVs, or any other type of message expansion. As with authenticated encryption, the main idea behind this methodology is that, whereas typical user data demonstrate patterns such as repeated bytes or...</p>
